      "html": "<p>Scientific name: Iheringichthys megalops Eigenmann &amp; Ward, 1907.</p><p>Family: Pimelodidae.</p><p>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2020).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1179",
      "html": "<p>South America: Paraná River basin. Type locality: Bahia Negra, Río Paraguay, Paraguay.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1179",
      "html": "<p>Unreported in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1179",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: Named after Hermann von Ihering, 1850-1930, who arrived in Brazil in 1880 and settled in Rio Grande, and was an expert in birds, fishes and molluscs. The specific epithet refers to its large (megale = large) eyes (ops = eyes).</p>"
    },
